A table's description tells where the table lies in the kernel's memory, besides its slots;
no result of a describing call is an object capability's address.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a description differs from the capability it describes
Witness: fuzz describe-every-type

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -927,6 +927,7 @@ static __attribute__((noinline)) int cap_info(const struct cap *cap, uint32_t *a
     }
     case CAP_CAPTABLE:
         arg[2] = ((const struct captable *)cap_object(cap))->nslots;
+        arg[3] = cap->a;
         break;
     case CAP_PROCESS:
         /* Its region slots, and the most a process may have here, an entry each: what OP_POOL_ALLOC holds a4 to. */
